      "why": "RE-PINNED 2026-09-12 when ko-bastion#127 shipped. This case was excluded because its error CLASS was nondeterministic: the same well-formed but nonexistent accession returned a 404 in one M0 recording and a 502-after-60.2s in another, and on 2026-09-12 it blocked a main deploy by moving 404 -> 502 between the local run and CI (run 34711440107). The cause was that koFetch waited without a bound, so a stalled EDGAR miss surfaced as somebody else's 5xx instead of the 404 the input deserves. koFetch is now bounded at 20s, under the 30s the upstream route declares, and a stall raises KoTimeoutError -- named, ours, and never a `ko.io API error (5xx)` line that this file could mistake for a contract.",
